WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Narrator] When you
think of Japanese cuisine,

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.010
a few foods come to mind.

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:07.160
Sushi, did you know that salmon
sushi is actually Norwegian?

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.700
- [Narrator] Yeah, we
did a story on that one.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.160
- [Narrator] Maybe you think of mochi?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.750
- [Narrator] We did that one, too.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.800
- [Narrator] And tempura, but, guess what?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.120
Tempura is actually a Portuguese dish.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.560
- [Narrator] Oh, boy, here we go.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.500
- [Narrator] The Japanese tempura
you know is done two ways:

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.220
either with seafood or with vegetables.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.900
- [Narrator] Right, and
the batter is light,

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.650
made with cold water,
wheat flour and egg.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.890
Pretty standard.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.950
- [Narrator] This tempura
can be found dating back

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.550
to the end of the 16th century in Japan.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.140
- [Narrator] But as we know,
Japan is much older than that.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.180
So, why did it suddenly show up?

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.420
The answer is:

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.320
- [Both] Portugal!

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.860
- [Narrator] Around 1543,

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.220
a Chinese ship with three
Portuguese sailors got off course

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.140
and landed in Japan on Tanegashima island.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.770
- [Narrator] Fast forward
a bit, and the Portuguese,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.430
because of this happy accident,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:01.210
are now trading goods, and
arms, with the Japanese.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.560
- [Narrator] Then, in 1639,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.660
the Portuguese were
kicked out of the country.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.330
A few things, however, remained,

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.680
including a dish of
battered and fried beans

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.680
called Peixinhos da Horta.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.330
- [Narrator] That's Manuela
Brandão, chef at Pap'Açôrda,

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:22.260
one of the best spots in Lisbon
to get Peixinhos da Horta.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.690
- [Narrator] Now, of course,
over the past 400 years,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.910
Japan has put its own spin on the dish,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.350
but, you know, it's a fun fact next time

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.250
somebody in your group orders tempura.

